1️⃣ FUNDAMENTALS:
thread:
A thread is the smallest unit of execution within a process that
performs a specific task independently.
One program = many tasks
Each task = one thread

🔹 Real-life Example
Mobile phone:
Playing music 🎵 → Thread 1
Downloading file ⬇ → Thread 2
WhatsApp notification 🔔 → Thread 3
Same app, multiple tasks → threads

2. What is Multithreading?
Multithreading is a Java feature that allows multiple threads to execute concurrently within a single program.
Java supports multithreading so that it can do many tasks at the same time and use the CPU efficiently.

Why Java supports multithreading?

.

🔹 Why Java supports multithreading?

CPU has multiple cores

Java wants maximum CPU utilization

Faster and responsive applications

3. Why Multithreading is Needed?
❌ Without Multithreading

Tasks execute one by one

Slow

Poor user experience

✅ With Multithreading

✔ Parallel execution
✔ Faster response
✔ Better performance

🔹 Real-Project Usage

Web server handles multiple users

Banking app handles multiple transactions

E-commerce site handles orders + payments + notifications

| Process             | Thread            |
| ------------------- | ----------------- |
| Independent program | Part of a process |
| Own memory          | Shared memory     |
| Heavyweight         | Lightweight       |
| Slow context switch | Fast              |
👉 Java uses threads because creating processes is expensive.

