13. What is a Daemon Thread?
🔹 Definition
A daemon thread is a background thread that provides services to user threads.
🔹 Key Rule
👉 JVM exits automatically when only daemon threads remain.

🔹 Examples of Daemon Threads
Garbage Collector (GC)
Background cleanup
Auto-save

🔹 Real-Life Analogy
Watchman in building
Once all people leave → watchman leaves
